      },
      "worked": "Let $R$ denote rain and $W$ a win. Use the rain and dry branches to find the total winning probability.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(R\\cap W)&=0.3\\times0.6=0.18\\\\P(W)&=0.3\\times0.6+0.7\\times0.25=0.355\\\\P(R\\mid W)&=\\frac{0.18}{0.355}=\\frac{36}{71}\\\\P(R\\mid W)&\\approx0.507\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
